WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
Paris 2024.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:06.110
The organisers list a budget
of 4.38 billion euros,

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.850
96 per cent of it private.

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.270
France's audit court
estimates public spending too:

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:18.470
3.02 billion euros on organisation,
and 3.63 billion on infrastructure.

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.290
Its verdict on the
long-term economic benefits:

7
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.430
at this stage, uncertain.

8
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.670
Is hosting a guaranteed profit?

9
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.430
Does the IOC pay for everything?

10
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.110
So why do countries still compete to host?

11
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.450
In this mission, you'll
sort the political,

12
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.030
economic and cultural factors
that shape who can host.

13
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.830
Then you'll see how FIFA's rules decided
which regions could bid for the 2026

14
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.990
World Cup.

15
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.490
Your mission: explain why countries
still compete to host the Games.
